<!-- The N.D. Cal. motion's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs) in the face of the
     typst template ({font}, Times New Roman; CAND-FORM-002, Civil L.R. 3-4(c)(2)(A)) at 12 pt (size 24 half points,
     footnotes too); Body Text in exact 24 pt line boxes (typst pitch-double, CAND-FORM-001 double spacing) with a
     half-inch first-line indent; headings, tables, caption, counsel, signature and footnote lines in 12 pt boxes
     (typst pitch-single, two to a numbered line), footnotes 7 pt apart (typst note-gap). docx/cand.lua writes every other paragraph's own
     spacing, the sections (letter paper, pleading paper: 1.5 in left, 1 in right, 60 pt top and bottom, 28 numbered lines; Civil L.R. 3-4(c)(1)-(2)), the footer with the page number,
     the paper's title and the case number (CAND-FORM-003) and the page numbers of the tables. Twips: 20 x pt. -->
<reference xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" base="xengine" size="24" body="480" single="240" indent="720" heading="240" heading-before="240" heading-after="240" note="240" note-after="140"/>
